-- The timeless ledger (w5): delay, recharge, and mana are columns, and a cast block's cost is a fold. Twin of w5-ledger.bqn.
-- Wand [Add Mana, SB, SB, Chainsaw], the whole block drawn. Add Mana credits inside the same barrier the block debits — the two writes share the additive family, so the §10 merge law takes both, order-free (the n2 machinery, spent on a resource).
-- The Chainsaw's negative recharge cancels the bolts' exactly: the rapid-fire trick is a ledger fact, no clock required; the negative net delay is data too — clamping to zero is the host's business at schedule time.
--! registry w5-ledger
--! expect mana = 69 0 0 0 0
--! expect delay = -7 0 0 0 0
--! expect recharge = 0 0 0 0 0

Wand , Mana += 30 * (#/ (Spell & AddMana)) ; Mana -= +/ ManaCost @ Spell
Wand , Delay = +/ CastDelay @ Spell
Wand , Recharge = +/ RechargeTime @ Spell
